diagnosis_text:
Affected component: DNS service (Bind9) on srv1 (10.5.0.4), which the PCs use as their resolver. Mechanism: Clients can reach the WAN by IP, but all domain lookups to 10.5.0.4 are refused, so browsers “spin” and then time out because names can’t be resolved. Localization: On pc1, /etc/resolv.conf points to 10.5.0.4. pc1 can ping WAN IPs (e.g., 203.0.113.5 on ispb), proving upstream routing/“internet line” is fine. A DNS test from pc1 returns “status: REFUSED, recursion requested but not available” from 10.5.0.4. On srv1, Bind is listening on 10.5.0.4:53, and its /etc/bind/named.conf explicitly sets “recursion no;” and is configured only as an authoritative server for a local zone, not as a caching/recursive resolver. R
